NSS_Region	Character	-	-	Region code ​
District	Character	-	-	District code ​
Stratum	Character	-	-	Coding for survey stratification ​
Sub_Stratum	Character	-	-	Sub-stratification code ​
Sub_Round	Character	-	-	Sub-round indicator ​
FOD_Sub_Region	Character	-	-	Field Office sub-region code ​
Sample_HH_No	Numeric	-	-	Household sample number ​
Person_Serial_No	Numeric	-	-	Person serial number within household ​
Relation_to_Head	Discrete	Character	-	Relationship category ​
Gender	Discrete	Character	1=Male, 2=Female, 3=Other	Gender of individual ​
Marital_Status	Discrete	Character	-	Marital status categories ​
Highest_Education	Discrete	Character	-	Highest education: categorical ​
Principal_Activity_Status	Discrete	Character	-	Occupation status: categorical ​
NIC_Industry_Code	Discrete	Numeric	2-digit code	Industry code per NIC 2008 ​
Member_Serial_No	Numeric	-	-	Household member serial number ​
Member_Age	Numeric	-	-	Age of household member ​
Informant_Serial_No	Numeric	-	-	Number of informant ​
Informant_Gender	Discrete	Character	1=Male, 2=Female, etc.	Gender of informant ​
Type_of_Day	Discrete	Character	Codes for day type	​
Response_Code	Numeric	-	-	Indicator for response: categorical ​
Activity_Member_Serial_No	Numeric	-	-	Serial no. for activity member ​
Activity_Member_Age	Numeric	-	Min: 6, Max: 118	Age while performing activity; mean: 35.88 ​
Activity_Serial_No	Numeric	-	-	Activity serial ​
Time_From	Character	Time	HH:MM format	Activity starting time ​
Time_To	Character	Time	HH:MM format	Activity ending time ​
Multiple_Activity_Flag	Boolean	-	1=Yes, 2=No	Multiple activities? ​
Simultaneous_Activity_Flag	Boolean	-	1=Yes, 2=No	Simultaneous activities? ​
Major_Activity_Flag	Boolean	-	1=Yes, 2=No	Was activity major? ​
Activity_Code_3Digit	Numeric	-	Coded 3-digit	Code for activity ​
Activity_Location	Character	-	-	Location where performed ​
Unpaid_Paid_Status	Discrete	Character	1=Unpaid, 2=Paid	Was activity paid/unpaid? ​
Enterprise_Type	Discrete	Character	-	Enterprise typology ​
NSC	Character	-	-	NSC variable ​
MULT	Character	-	-	MULT variable ​
Key specifics:

Age is numeric, continuous, min 6, max 118, mean 35.88, width 3, valid/invalid counts noted.

Day of the week is discrete: 1=Monday, ..., 7=Sunday. Distribution is even, categorical codes used.

Categorical/discrete variables use meaningful codes (e.g., Gender, Day of Week, Paid/Unpaid, etc.)

